From a05d1dca51ba36099d5b1b3186e4fe75c247bc30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "JQE Chief Engineer (Claude)" <jqe-bot@example.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 19:41:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/37] fix: separate data/ source package from cache runtime
 output in .gitignore
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The blanket 'data/' rule would have silently excluded this milestone's
entire data package from version control the moment its files were
added — the exact bug flagged in Milestone 1. Fixed by never routing
cache output through data/ at all: the candle cache lives under a new
sibling directory (cache/, git-ignored) instead, mirroring the
existing logs/ convention (a runtime-output directory separate from
the core/ source that writes to it).

Also dedupes the file's several repeated entries while rewriting it.
---
 .gitignore | 30 ++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index ec02ca6..9795536 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,27 +1,10 @@
 # Python
 __pycache__/
-*.pyc
+*.py[cod]
 
-# Virtual Environment
+# Virtual environment
 venv/
 
-# Logs
-logs/*.log
-
-# Reports
-reports/
-
-# Data
-data/
-
-# Environment variables
-.env# Virtual environment
-venv/
-
-# Python cache
-__pycache__/
-*.py[cod]
-
 # Environment variables
 .env
 
@@ -35,6 +18,13 @@ __pycache__/
 logs/
 *.log
 
+# Reports
+reports/
+
+# Runtime candle cache (data/ is a tracked source package — see
+# data/storage.py; only its runtime SQLite output is ignored here)
+cache/
+
 # Coverage
 .coverage
 htmlcov/
@@ -46,4 +36,4 @@ dist/
 
 # OS files
 .DS_Store
-Thumbs.db
\ No newline at end of file
+Thumbs.db
-- 
2.43.0

